-- title:
--   Twisted centraliser of a diagonal element with unit norm difference
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be fields with $L$ a finite-dimensional Galois extension of $K$, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $A$ be a commutative $K$-algebra and put $E = L \otimes_K A$, viewed as an $A$-algebra through the right factor. Write $\sigma_E$ for the automorphism `sigmaTensor K L A σ` of $E$ attached to $\sigma$, and let $\sigma$ act on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ by applying $\sigma_E$ to each matrix entry, i.e. by the homomorphism [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaGL K L A σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L202). Let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$ have $\delta_{10} = \delta_{01} = 0$ and suppose that $N(\delta_{00}) - N(\delta_{11})$ is a unit of $A$, where $N =$ `Algebra.norm A` is the norm of $E$ over $A$. Then for $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E)$, the condition $t\,\delta\,(\sigma t)^{-1} = \delta$ defining membership in the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser [`AutomorphicForm.twistedCentralizer K L A σ δ`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L220) holds if and only if $t_{10} = 0$, $t_{01} = 0$, and both $t_{00}$ and $t_{11}$ lie in the image of $A \to E$, $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$ (the range of `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight`).
--
--   This identifies the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser of a diagonal element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ whose two diagonal norms differ by a unit with the diagonal torus of $\mathrm{GL}_2(A)$, sitting in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K A)$ through the right factor; the hypotheses on $A$ are uniform, so the result applies equally to local, archimedean and adelic bases. It is used in the comparison of twisted orbital integrals for such regular diagonal classes and in the identification of the twisted centraliser of a diagonal unit matrix with the image of the centraliser of its norm.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_mem_twistedCentralizer_iff_of_diagonal_of_isUnit_norm_sub_norm.lean

import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
